Private copy "sp" of the chip-set RTL: a deliberate fault against p. 345, used by the
implementation-red record of P7.6-CIAA in appF-cia-system. It is made by
`make sp-rtl-<core>` from a copy of the pinned submodule's src/minimig-aga/ and never
changes the submodule.

This copy is NOT a page-conforming implementation. p. 345 says that after eight CNT
pulses an interrupt is generated and that the SP flag follows the serial port; here the key
code no longer reaches the interrupt controller's serial input in ciaa.v (`.ser`), so SP
stays 0 after a key code although every timing clause of P7.5-WINDOW holds. It exists to
show that P7.6-CIAA can print FAIL on a run whose timing clauses hold.

--- a/ciaa.v
+++ b/ciaa.v
@@ -319,7 +319,7 @@
   .tb(tb),
   .alrm(alrm),
   .flag(1'b0),
-  .ser(keystrobe | ser_tx_irq),
+  .ser(ser_tx_irq),
   .data_in(data_in),
   .data_out(icr_out),
   .irq(irq)
